target:    src/Schema/Schema.php
gate:      php tests/db-floor-metadata-test.php
kind:      introduce-defect
expect:    compares a database server version with version_compare()
rationale: Enforce the floor the obvious way, which bricks every MariaDB install there is. MariaDB reports $wpdb->db_version() as 5.5.5-10.x - a string that begins 5.5.5 for legacy compatibility - so version_compare(db_version(), '5.6', '<') is TRUE on all of them, and all of them are inside the supported floor. ADR-2's C12 amendment calls this a blocker in so many words. It is pinned as a mutation rather than a sentence because correcting the floor line in the readme is exactly what prompts someone to go and enforce it.
---
--- a/src/Schema/Schema.php
+++ b/src/Schema/Schema.php
@@ -702,6 +702,10 @@
      */
     public static function targetCollation(wpdb $core): string
     {
+        if (version_compare($core->db_version(), '5.6', '<')) {
+            return 'utf8_general_ci';
+        }
+
         $collation = $core->get_var($core->prepare(
             "SELECT COLLATION_NAME FROM information_schema.COLUMNS
               WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA = DATABASE() AND TABLE_NAME = %s AND COLUMN_NAME = 'user_login'",
